NAME
       morse - write text as Morse code, or read it back (Cyber Range)

SYNOPSIS
       morse [FILE]
       morse -d [FILE]

DESCRIPTION
       Morse code writes each letter and digit as short (.) and long (-)
       signals. morse writes the letters of a word separated by single spaces
       and the words separated by " / ". With -d it reads dots and dashes the
       same way and prints the letters (in capitals); a group it doesn't know
       shows as ?.

       Besides A-Z and 0-9 it knows { } _ - . , ? ! / = : ' and @ (the curly
       braces use the bracket signals -.--. and -.--.-).

       morse is a Cyber Range practice tool; it works only inside the range.

OPTIONS
       -d, --decode
              Read Morse code and print the text.

EXAMPLES
           echo 'sos' | morse
           echo '... --- ...' | morse -d

SEE ALSO
       base64(1), tr(1)
